# The backend images and the three frontend images all build from the repo ROOT, because
# they copy shared code (packages/core, packages/ui) that sits outside their own folder.
# Without this file every one of those builds ships the whole working tree: .git, three
# node_modules trees, .nuxt, .venv and the coverage files came to roughly 615 MB and over
# twenty minutes just to hand the context to the daemon.
#
# Anything a Dockerfile actually copies must stay: packages/core, packages/ui,
# services/*/app, services/*/alembic, services/*/requirements*.txt and the frontend
# sources including their package.json and package-lock.json. Check the Dockerfile before
# adding a line here.
#
# services/identity builds from services/identity instead, so it reads that folder's own
# .dockerignore, not this one.

.git
.gitignore
.github

# Dependency and build output. Every image installs its own inside the build.
**/node_modules
**/.nuxt
**/.output
**/.nitro
**/.venv
**/venv
**/*.egg-info

# Python and tooling caches.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.coverage*
**/htmlcov
**/.DS_Store

# Real secrets. Runtime config arrives through env_file / the platform's env vars, never
# baked into a layer. The examples are text and stay.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Docs, notes and local scratch. No image reads them.
docs
graphify-out
scripts
tests
.claude
*.pdf
# Root-level .md only: docker matches a slash-free pattern against the top level, so
# packages/core/README.md and the services' READMEs are untouched.
*.md
